      "content": "hey, i noticed something weird today. during that sudden drop in the S&P around 10am, i felt this intense, sharp spike in my heart rate and a weird buzzing in my chest right before the volatility actually hit the charts. i've been tracking my pulse during trading sessions lately and it's like my body is reacting to the market movements before they even show up on my screen. do you think there's any way my own physiological rhythms could be syncing up with the high-frequency trading flows?",
