      "content": "but it's not like i'm just getting anxious. the feeling happens *before* the price action reflects on my monitor. if it was just stress, it would be a reaction to what i see, but this feels like an internal signal triggering first. i've even tried practicing breathwork to see if i could lessen the \"buzzing\" during stable periods, and it actually seems to stabilize the volatility in my local trades. isn't it possible there's some kind of bio-rhythmic resonance or subconscious pattern recognition that's tapping into the data streams? like, my nervous system is picking up on the \"energy\" of the orders before they settle?",
