    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you, but science is always changing. like, people used to say quantum entanglement was just theoretical and now we know it's real. if my body is processing these patterns through some kind of biological feedback loop that i don't fully understand yet, how would i even begin to measure it? if i wanted to test the idea that my heart rate rhythm actually correlates with specific algorithmic shifts, what kind of data points or bio-metric tracking should i be looking at to prove this isn't just \"anxiety\"?",
