      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While past science did evolve, there is currently no known mechanism allowing human physiology to emit measurable signals that precede High-Frequency Trading algorithmic shifts by minutes or more. To scientifically test this, you would need real-time ECG data correlated with second-by-second price feeds, which would almost certainly show your heart rate spiking *after* your awareness of the price move, not before, due to the lag in neural processing. The closest you can get to objective proof is a large-scale study totaling thousands of sessions, but until data shows a consistent causal link between your pulse and order flow, the sensation remains an anecdotal example of heightened physiological awareness rather than a biological influence on the market.",
